WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.482
Now the function receives two values: sales and costs.

00:00:04.482 --> 00:00:12.542
When we call profit_report with twelve hundred fifty and nine hundred, those numbers flow into the two parameters.

00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:19.037
The function subtracts costs from sales, giving a profit of three hundred fifty dollars,

00:00:19.037 --> 00:00:21.401
then formats the result as money.

00:00:22.195 --> 00:00:25.827
Try a second call with two thousand and sixteen hundred.

00:00:25.827 --> 00:00:30.137
The same function should produce four hundred dollars in profit.

00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:37.311
This is a common analytics pattern: define the metric once, then reuse it with different records.
